+# Agent Note: Add a second main column inside the centre for a plugin workbench
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-10-second-main-column.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A study-workbench plugin needs its working surface beside the native conversation in the same window: left study area, right conversation. The shipped frame offers three placements and none fits:
+
+| Placement | Why it is not enough |
+|---|---|
+| Left `sidebar` | 264–420px navigation column; the occupant owns it and would replace navigation |
+| Right `rightbar` | Opens on the right (reversed direction), is Session-scoped, and disappears when a global panel replaces the conversation |
+| A global main panel | Replaces the conversation instead of standing beside it |
+
+A fourth grid track would fix the direction but forces every column solve, resize handle, and responsive rule to price another track. The upstream layout specs assert the three-track template directly.
+
+## Decision
+
+Add a root-scoped `studyleft` single slot inside the centre column, drawn left of `main`:
+
+| Item | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| Rendering | `CenterColumn` becomes a horizontal flex row: `[studyleft wrapper][mainPanel]`; the frame's grid template is unchanged |
+| Width source | `ctx.layout.setLeftmain(px)` writes `layoutInfo.leftmain`; 0 hides the column |
+| Clamp | Rendered width is `clampWidth(leftmain, 320, centre − 400)` |
+| Visibility | Hidden below a 1024px frame or when the centre is under 720px (400px conversation + 320px column); no frame-level notice, the occupant's single-page entry is the fallback |
+| Handle | The frame draws one handle at `sidebar + rendered width`; dragging left widens the study column |
+| Owner props | `{ width, savedWidth, viewportWidth, canShow }`; `width` is the rendered value, `savedWidth` is the preference the occupant persists so a squeeze cannot overwrite it |
+| Persistence | None in the frame. `leftmain` resets on reload like every other layout preference; the occupant restores its own copy through `setLeftmain` |
+| Locale | Zero new keys and no frame controls |
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **A fourth grid track**: every `computeColumns` caller, the template string, and the drag/resize tests would learn the track; the centre-internal flex split leaves the existing three-track solve and its specs intact.
+- **Reuse the right `rightbar`**: reversed direction, Session-scoped rendering, and covered by a global panel — the route this workbench replaced.
+- **Fall back to the left `sidebar`**: replaces the navigation column outright and is far narrower than a workbench.
+- **Persist the width in the layout store**: the frame owns geometry, not plugin preferences; keeping Storage out of `ui-layout` lets the occupant version its own key.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The centre's own children are now a flex row; `mainPanel` keeps `flex: 1` and `min-width: 0`, and any future centre child must account for the row direction.
+- Below 1024px or beside a wide right panel the study column disappears while its occupant stays mounted only as a single page; a user who relied on the side-by-side view gets no in-frame explanation.
+- The centre can be temporarily narrower than its protected 400px while the JS solve lags a live resize; the conversation absorbs the difference for one frame.
+- Upstream specs for the grid template and column solve are untouched; the new slot adds one declaration, one store field, one service method, and one handle.
